From: SAGIT Port <sagit@local>
Subject: [PATCH] sagit: disable PAN

PAN is an ARMv8.1 feature and Kryo 280 (A73/A53) does not implement it.
SWEET.h enables __ARM_PAN_AVAILABLE__, and arm_init() then executes
"msr pan, #1" unconditionally, which traps as an undefined instruction on
this core.  Drop the define for SAGIT the same way 16K pages are dropped.
---
 pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SAGIT.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SAGIT.h b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SAGIT.h
--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SAGIT.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SAGIT.h
@@ -25,6 +25,12 @@
  * ID_AA64MMFR0_EL1.TGran16 is 1 on Kryo 280: 16K translation is unsupported.
  * SWEET.h supplies shared board definitions, but SAGIT must use 4K pages.
  */
 #undef __ARM_16K_PG__
 
+/*
+ * PAN is ARMv8.1; Kryo 280 does not implement it, and arm_init() executes
+ * "msr pan, #1" as soon as __ARM_PAN_AVAILABLE__ is defined.
+ */
+#undef __ARM_PAN_AVAILABLE__
+
 #endif /* ! _PEXPERT_ARM64_SAGIT_H */
